# Agentic test ladder (ProjectB)

After C++ or match-flow wiring changes, **ask the user to recompile and restart the editor manually**. Do not run Tier 1 as part of agent task completion — it is slow, error-prone (Live Coding conflicts, long UBT runs), and blocks the agent loop.

Optional scripted tiers live in `Scripts/Test/` when the user or CI wants them.

## Tier 1 — compile gate (optional; user/CI only)

```powershell
cd "E:\Unreal Projects\ProjectB\Scripts\Test"
.\Run-Tier.ps1 -Tier 1
```

- Target: **`LyraEditor`** or **`ProjectBEditor`** (alias of `LyraEditorTarget` in `Source/ProjectBEditor.Target.cs`).
- Exit 0 = compile OK. Non-zero = fix before claiming done.
- Path check only: `.\Run-Tier.ps1 -Tier 1 -ValidateOnly`
- Engine override: `$env:UE_ENGINE_ROOT = 'E:\Github\UnrealEngine'`

**Agent rule:** Do **not** run Tier 1. After C++ edits, tell the user to rebuild (editor closed or Live Coding off) and verify in editor/PIE as needed.

## Tier 2 / 3 — when applicable (optional)

| Situation | Tier |
|-----------|------|
| Standalone / packaged experience regression | 2 (needs `ProjectB.exe`) |
| Core-loop sub-step (11-1, 11-2, …) | 3 CQTest filter `Breakaway.CoreLoop.<step>` |

Full design: `Plugins/GameFeatures/BreakawayCore/Docs/Agent_Testing_Ladder.md`

## Reporting

Include in the task summary:
- Whether C++ changed and user was asked to recompile/restart editor
- PIE or manual verification results if the user ran them
- Do not block task completion on Tier 1 exit code
